Competitors like @nick_saraev and @arshman capture immediate retention within the first 2 seconds using high-stakes negative framing or direct comparative hooks (e.g., "Forget ElevenLabs. Instead, use this free alternative...", "This guy accidentally gained access to 7,000 cameras..."). In contrast, @garvit.irl uses slow conversational warmups ("Tumhe pta hai...", "Khair us waqt to ho nahi paya but..."), which slows down retention before the core value is delivered.

2. Tool-Specific Tactical Utility vs. Generalized Concepts
Top-performing creators showcase specific, actionable workflows featuring exact tools and plugins (e.g., Claude Code design skills, OmniVoice, Replit Design Agent, 3D AI renders). While @garvit.irl touches on relevant topics like prompt writing and Emergent funnels, the delivery leans towards abstract discussion rather than rapid, step-by-step problem-solving tutorials that drive massive saves and shares.

3. Static Post Drag vs. Reel Dominance
@garvit.irl averages only 31 likes on static posts compared to 315 likes on Reels (a 10x difference). Across the entire competitor landscape, 100% of high-performing, viral reach is captured strictly through Reels. Continuing to publish static image/carousel formats dilutes distribution and lowers overall account velocity.


